{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>From days to days.</b> This teaches that a person must inspect tefillin once every twelve months. It says here ימים וגו׳ — these are the words of Bet Hillel. Bet Shammai say: they never need to be inspected. Hillel the Elder says: these are the tefillin of my father's mother. And we learned there in Chelek: Yehudah ben Batera stood on his feet and said: I am of the grandchildren of the dead whom Yehezkel revived, and these are the tefillin that my father left me from them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "ב״ה and ב״ש resolved as Bet Hillel and Bet Shammai. החיה is rendered literally as 'revived'; the reference is to Yehezkel's vision of the dry bones. The phrase תפילין של אבי אמא is understood as 'the tefillin of my father's mother.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:35.758563401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}